# an ending
@title Silence
@bg field
@mood grief

narrate He walked north alone, ahead of them, and stood at the edge of the hole in the field.
corin resolute "End it."
narrate And the hole took what was left of him and ended the Fever, everywhere, forever.
narrate It worked. It worked completely.
narrate And there was no one left who could say who had asked, because the only man who knew was standing in a field with a clean hand and no memory at all.
bryn grieving "..."
narrate Bryn found the note and read it and could not speak for a day.
narrate The Fever ended. Nobody ever knew why. In the end the accepted position was that the Grey Fever had run its course.
narrate Corin lived another forty years on the high ground in the Mire, and was a quiet man, and was well liked, and could never explain why a sentence about a man with mud to his knees giving a boy half a loaf made him cry in a way he could not account for.
narrate He survived it. He got up anyway. Every day, for forty years, in a garden, on the high ground, reading a ledger about a man he did not know and believing it anyway.

@ending silence
